4 63.2, 1147.8 52 M1140.3 70.4 C1142 67.6, 1144.6 65.8, 1149 60.3 M1140.1 70.2 C1141.7 68.2, 1143.7 66.6, 1147.5 61.7" fill="none" stroke="#b2f2bb" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M1047.7 20.1 C1066.6 18.5, 1085.7 19.8, 1139.1 18.5 M1046.9 20.9 C1081.2 19.3, 1118.8 19.2, 1137.2 20.9 M1138 20 C1143.9 18.4, 1149.2 23.1, 1146 31.3 M1136.3 21.6 C1146.1 20.3, 1148.6 25.1, 1148.7 28.7 M1149.6 28 C1148.4 43.2, 1147.7 53.2, 1148.2 61.2 M1147.6 29.7 C1147.8 37.4, 1149.1 46.7, 1148.8 60.6 M1148 60 C1149.5 66.4, 1143.2 69.3, 1136.2 71.4 M1149.5 58.5 C1147.8 65.4, 1145.6 70.6, 1137.8 71.4 M1139.3 70.9 C1114 69.1, 1092.4 70, 1046.6 71.4 M1137.5 69.7 C1113.6 69.6, 1091 69.3, 1045.3 70.8 M1046 70 C1038 70.6, 1035 67.9, 1035.4 58 M1047.6 71.3 C1037.5 71.9, 1037.4 66.1, 1034.9 62.1 M1036.8 60.9 C1036.7 50.6, 1035.5 43.4, 1035.6 30.3 M1036.8 60.9 C1036.8 50.9, 1035.5 41.6, 1036.1 29.5 M1036 30 C1034.7 23.5, 1040.9 18, 1047.4 18.1 M1036.1 30.6 C1035.9 21.8, 1039.3 22.1, 1047.3 18.4 M1046 20 C1046 20, 1046 20, 1046 20 M1046 20 C1046 20, 1046 20, 1046 20" fill="none" stroke="#1e1e1e" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><text class="wb-text-title" x="1092" y="49.4" text-anchor="middle">scats (v2)</text></g><g class="wb-connector-label"><path d="M 450.5 25 L 492.5 25 Q 496.5 25 496.5 29 L 496.5 43 Q 496.5 47 492.5 47 L 450.5 47 Q 446.5 47 446.5 43 L 446.5 29 Q 446.5 25 450.5 25 Z" fill="#fcfcfb" fill-opacity="0.94"/><text class="wb-text-connector" x="471.5" y="39.5" text-anchor="middle">先应用</text></g><g class="wb-connector-label"><path d="M 616 96 L 748 96 Q 752 96 752 100 L 752 130 Q 752 134 748 134 L 616 134 Q 612 134 612 130 L 612 100 Q 612 96 616 96 Z" fill="#fcfcfb" fill-opacity="0.94"/><text class="wb-text-connector" x="682" y="110.5" text-anchor="middle">和 Alice 的操作做 OT</text><text class="wb-text-connector" x="682" y="126.5" text-anchor="middle">位置 3 变成 4</text></g></svg></figure>
<p>如果两个人都在同一个位置插入呢？比如都在 <code>pos=0</code>。这时系统需要一个确定性的 tie-breaker / deterministic ordering rule，比如按服务端接收顺序，再结合 <code>user_id</code> 或 <code>op_id</code> 做稳定排序。重点不是规则多聪明，而是所有副本都必须按同一个规则得到同一个顺序。<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-sandbox-ot" id="user-content-fnref-sandbox-ot" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">6</a></sup></p>
<p>OT 的难点在实现。你不只要处理 insert vs insert，还要处理：</p>
<ul>
<li>insert vs delete</li>
<li>delete vs insert</li>
<li>delete vs delete</li>
<li>format vs insert</li>
<li>format vs delete</li>
</ul>
<p>操作类型越多，变换函数越多，边界条件也越多。这就是 OT 难调试的地方。<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-systemdr" id="user-content-fnref-systemdr" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">7</a></sup></p>
<p>那为什么还用 OT？因为 Google Docs 这种产品本来就需要中央服务端：</p>
<ul>
<li>要做权限检查。</li>
<li>要保存历史。</li>
<li>要做审计和恢复。</li>
<li>多端同步要有权威版本。</li>
</ul>
<p>既然服务端已经在链路中间，让服务端负责排序和变换是合理的工程选择。<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-designgurus-arch" id="user-content-fnref-designgurus-arch" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">8</a></sup><sup><a href="#user-content-fn-systemdr" id="user-content-fnref-systemdr-2" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">7</a></sup></p>
<hr>
<h2 id="7-crdt另一条路把顺序藏进数据结构">7. CRDT：另一条路，把顺序藏进数据结构</h2>
<p>CRDT 是另一类协同编辑方案，在很多新协同系统和离线优先应用里很常见。<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-sdhandbook" id="user-content-fnref-sdhandbook-3" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">1</a></sup></p>
<p>它和 OT 的思路不一样。OT 说：“位置过期了，我帮你变换操作。”CRDT 说：“我干脆不用容易过期的普通位置。”</p>
<p>在文本 CRDT 里，每个字符都有一个稳定的、有序的 ID，也就是 stable position identifier。你可以粗略理解成一个可以无限插入的小数位置。比如：</p>
<pre class="shiki github-light" style="background-color:#fff;color:#24292e" tabindex="0" data-language="text"><code><span class="line"><span>c(1) a(2) t(3)</span></span></code></pre>
<p>Alice 在开头插入 <code>s</code>，给它一个排在 <code>c(1)</code> 前面的 ID：</p>
<pre class="shiki github-light" style="background-color:#fff;color:#24292e" tabindex="0" data-language="text"><code><span class="line"><span>s(0.5)</span></span></code></pre>
<p>Bob 在结尾插入 <code>s</code>，给它一个排在 <code>t(3)</code> 后面的 ID：</p>
<pre class="shiki github-light" style="background-color:#fff;color:#24292e" tabindex="0" data-language="text"><code><span class="line"><span>s(3.5)</span></span></code></pre>
<p>不管两个操作以什么顺序到达，只要所有副本都按 ID 排序，最后都是：</p>
<pre class="shiki github-light" style="background-color:#fff;color:#24292e" tabindex="0" data-language="text"><code><span class="line"><span>s(0.5) c(1) a(2) t(3) s(3.5)</span></span></code></pre>
<p>也就是 <code>scats</code>。<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-sandbox-crdt" id="user-content-fnref-sandbox-crdt" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">9</a></sup></p>
<figure class="whiteboard-diagram" data-diagram-type="flowchart" style="--wb-natural-width: 1266px"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="-8 -8 1266 266" width="1266" height="266" role="img" aria-labelledby="wb-3youun-3-title wb-3youun-3-desc"><title id="wb-3youun-3-title">Diagram: s(0.5), c(1), a(2), t(3), s(3.5), …</title><desc id="wb-3youun-3-desc">s(0.5) → c(1); c(1) → a(2); a(2) → t(3); t(3) → s(3.5); s(0.5) → c(1); c(1) → a(2); a(2) → t(3); t(3) → s(3.5); 副本 1：先收到 Alice，再收到 Bob → 按 ID 排序后结果相同; 副本 2：先收到 Bob，再收到 Alice → 按 ID 排序后结果相同</desc><g class="wb-group"><path d="M25.4 12.1 C164 10.7, 303.6 10.2, 593 11.3 C606.3 15, 608 20.1, 609.3 26.6 C609.4 55.3, 607.9 78.3, 610.9 106.7 C611.4 120, 604.3 125.3, 591.1 124.9 C458.7 120.8, 321 122.7, 26.3 125.2 C20.1 124, 12.1 122.5, 11.6 111.4 C11.7 77.8, 16 43.9, 14.9 27.1 C15 19.5, 18.5 9.5, 27.1 9.7 C26 12, 26 12, 26 12" fill="#f1f3f5" stroke="none"/><path d="M26.3 12.2 C223.1 11.9, 421.5 12.2, 594.4 11.5 M594 12 C603.8 10.8, 608.7 16.5, 607.6 26.7 M608.2 25.4 C607.1 55.1, 608.8 85.3, 608.7 109.7 M608 110 C608.8 119.9, 603.2 124.4, 594.2 124.3 M593.9 124.3 C475.3 124.8, 355.3 124.4, 26.4 123.6 M26 124 C17.8 124.1, 10.9 118.8, 12.6 110.3 M12.4 109.8 C11.2 92.5, 13.2 74.8, 11.6 25.8 M12 26 C12.2 17, 17.3 12.8, 27 11.3 M26 12 C26 12, 26 12, 26 12" fill="none" stroke="#868e96" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-dasharray="7 6"/></g><g class="wb-group"><path d="M657.4 13.2 C883.5 12.5, 1110.2 11.7, 1223.7 13 C1232.1 14.6, 1235.2 15, 1239.3 28.4 C1235.5 46.4, 1233.7 60.9, 1238.1 107.7 C1237.8 122.9, 1230.9 124.4, 1226.9 127.4 C1020.5 120.4, 818.5 121.4, 656.3 122.7 C649.7 123.6, 640.2 115.9, 642.4 108.9 C640 87.8, 641.2 67.3, 638.7 26.6 C644.8 17.4, 650.1 12.9, 657.9 14.7 C656 12, 656 12, 656 12" fill="#f1f3f5" stroke="none"/><path d="M656.4 11.9 C783.2 11.4, 909.5 12, 1224.3 11.7 M1224 12 C1234.5 10.8, 1237.3 17.9, 1239.2 24.9 M1236.9 26.4 C1238.1 50.4, 1238 74.3, 1238.3 110.2 